    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n#   Datasets:⟨3⟩\n* * *\nDuplicated from hcislab/digital-twin⟨28⟩\n![⟨29⟩]\n ![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/664ddfff6beee47c792f5836/3uKjWlfj_TAWY2VJLbQNN.png) ⟨30⟩\nHCIS-Lab⟨30⟩\n/\ndigital-twin⟨31⟩\nlike 0\nFollow\n![⟨32⟩] Human-centered Intelligent System Lab 8\nTags:  digital-twin ⟨33⟩ usd ⟨34⟩ isaac-sim ⟨35⟩ lighting ⟨36⟩\nLicense:\ncc-by-nc-4.0\n Dataset card ⟨31⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨37⟩ Community ⟨38⟩\nDataset Viewer\nThe dataset viewer is not available because its heuristics could not detect any supported data files⟨39⟩. You can try uploading⟨40⟩ some data files, or configuring⟨41⟩ the data files location manually.\n  * Contents⟨42⟩\n  * Usage⟨43⟩\n  * Notes⟨44⟩\n  * Citation⟨45⟩\n  * License⟨46⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨47⟩ Room 305 Digital Twin \nA USD digital twin of NYCU Room 305 (lighting scene), built by the **Human-centered Intelligent System Lab (hcislab)** — GitHub @HCIS-Lab⟨48⟩. Authored for **NVIDIA Isaac Sim 5.1**.\n**Lab links:** GitHub @HCIS-Lab⟨48⟩ · HF @hcislab⟨49⟩\n##   ⟨42⟩ Contents \n\n```\nnycu_light_collider.usd    # main scene — open this in Isaac Sim (geometry + colliders + materials + lights)\nnycu_lights.usdz           # referenced geometry + textures (center.jpg, Translucent_Glass_Tinted.jpg)\n\n```\n\n`nycu_light_collider.usd` references `nycu_lights.usdz` by a **relative** path, so the two files must stay side by side. `snapshot_download` keeps them together automatically.\nScene stats (loaded in Isaac Sim 5.1): 443 meshes (~188k points), 419 materials / 459 shaders, a `DomeLight` + `RectLight`. Approx extent 12.1 × 7.0 × 3.4 m.\n##   ⟨43⟩ Usage \n\n```\nfrom huggingface_hub import snapshot_download\n\npath = snapshot_download(\n    repo_id=\"hcislab/digital-twin\",\n    repo_type=\"dataset\",\n)\n# open path/nycu_light_collider.usd in Isaac Sim 5.1\n\n```\n\nIn Isaac Sim (Python):\n\n```\nimport omni.usd\nomni.usd.get_context().open_stage(f\"{path}/nycu_light_collider.usd\")\n\n```\n\n##   ⟨44⟩ Notes \n  * Textures are bundled inside `nycu_lights.usdz` and resolve via relative paths — verified self-contained with `UsdUtils.ComputeAllDependencies`.\n  * Two references resolve **at runtime** in Isaac Sim / Omniverse and are intentionally not bundled:\n    * `OmniGlass.mdl` — Omniverse stock material library.\n    * A Cloudy dome-light HDR served from the Omniverse content CDN. Materials and dome lighting need an Omniverse asset connection / cache to display fully; geometry and the `RectLight` load without it.\n  * Verified to open cleanly in Isaac Sim 5.1 from a fresh download.\n\n\n##   ⟨45⟩ Citation \nIf you use this digital twin, please cite it:\n\n```\n@misc{hcislab_room305_2026,\n  title        = {Room 305 Digital Twin},\n  author       = {{Human-centered Intelligent System Lab}},\n  year         = {2026},\n  howpublished = {Hugging Face dataset},\n  url          = {https://huggingface.co/datasets/hcislab/digital-twin},\n  note         = {NVIDIA Isaac Sim 5.1 USD digital twin}\n}\n\n```\n\nA machine-readable `CITATION.cff` is included (Hugging Face renders a \"Cite this\" entry from it).\n##   ⟨46⟩ License \n**CC BY-NC 4.0** (Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0⟨50⟩).\n  * ✅ Share and adapt for **non-commercial** research/education, **with attribution** (cite as above).\n  * ❌ **No commercial use** without separate permission from the lab. For commercial licensing, contact **hcislab01@gmail.com**.\n\n\nNote: the referenced `OmniGlass.mdl` and dome-light HDR are NVIDIA Omniverse assets governed by their own licenses; they are not redistributed here.\nCopy to bucket new \n\nDownloads last month\n    58\nTotal file size: 2.4 MB\n##  Collection including HCIS-Lab/digital-twin\n#### HCIS Digital Twin Collection A collection of the dataset and simulation • 1 item • Updated 23 days ago ⟨51⟩\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨52⟩ Privacy⟨53⟩ About⟨54⟩ Careers⟨55⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
